{"name":"Aftercare","hex":"#85c0cd","fetched":"2026-10-16","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"aftercare","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The care given to a patient during recovery from an operation or after hospitalization.","Services and support offered to a customer for the goods or service they have purchased."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/aftercare"}],"entries":[{"title":"Aftercare (BDSM)","blocks":[{"text":"Aftercare refers to the process of providing emotional, psychological, or physical support to participants following BDSM activities. These activities can be mentally, emotionally, or physically intense, often leaving participants in need of comfort, reassurance, or physical tenderness. Aftercare may also involve a review or debriefing of the session to reflect on the experience and address any concerns or successes."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/54/Hug_it_out_%2852987500111%29.jpg/330px-Hug_it_out_%2852987500111%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Aftercare_(BDSM)","wikidata":"Q4690709"},{"title":"Aftercare (album)","blocks":[{"text":"Aftercare (stylized in all uppercase) is the second studio album from American singer-songwriter Nessa Barrett. The album was released on November 15, 2024, by Warner Records. A deluxe edition featuring 6 bonus tracks was released on February 7, 2025. Barrett stated that Aftercare was inspired by exploring \"love, sex and the aftermath\" and was intended to empower listeners to feel \"confident and comfortable with themselves and sex.\"\nHer main inspirations for the album include Tommy Genesis and Artemas who both feature the album, along with Lana Del Rey, Billie Eilish, Charli XCX, Melanie Martinez, and The Neighbourhood. Musically, Aftercare incorporates aspects of electro-pop, alt-pop, and dark-pop."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/e/e0/Nessa_Barrett_-_Aftercare.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Aftercare_(album)","wikidata":"Q131418294"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/54/Hug_it_out_%2852987500111%29.jpg/500px-Hug_it_out_%2852987500111%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/54/Hug_it_out_%2852987500111%29.jpg/1280px-Hug_it_out_%2852987500111%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/54/Hug_it_out_%2852987500111%29.jpg/500px-Hug_it_out_%2852987500111%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Post-flogging-demonstration embrace/aftercare at Folsom Street East Fair 2023","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AHug_it_out_(52987500111).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/e/e0/Nessa_Barrett_-_Aftercare.png/250px-Nessa_Barrett_-_Aftercare.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/e/e0/Nessa_Barrett_-_Aftercare.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/e/e0/Nessa_Barrett_-_Aftercare.png/250px-Nessa_Barrett_-_Aftercare.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ANessa_Barrett_-_Aftercare.png"}],"sounds":{"aftercare":[{"type":"audio/wav","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/4/44/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Wodencafe-aftercare.wav?utm_source=en.wiktionary.org&utm_campaign=rest&utm_content=original"},{"type":"audio/mpeg","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/4/44/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Wodencafe-aftercare.wav/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Wodencafe-aftercare